Provenance of vendored C++ source files in src/
================================================

The following files in src/ are derived from the FAUST project
(Faster Annotation Using Shape-constrained Trees):

  cpPmden.cpp
  tautstring.cpp
  kkuiper.cpp
  cppApprox.cpp
  local_density.cpp
  medianAbsoluteDeviation.cpp
  rQuantile.cpp

FAUST is authored by the Gottardo Lab (RGLab) and is available at:
  https://github.com/RGLab/FAUST

FAUST is licensed under GPL (>= 3).  The taut-string density estimation
algorithm in cpPmden.cpp and tautstring.cpp is identified in the upstream
FAUST source as a C++ port of the R package ftnonpar 0.1-88 by Laurie Davies
and Arne Kovac (https://cran.r-project.org/package=ftnonpar).

The file src/faust.h is a minimal package-local header containing only the
stringInfo structure and the cpPmden() declaration needed by the vendored
files.  It was written for stimgate based on the FAUST source and carries the
same GPL (>= 3) licence.

The file src/stimgate_faust.h is also a package-local header written for
stimgate, similarly GPL (>= 3).

The file src/stimgate_cppmden.cpp is a cpp11 R-interface wrapper written for
stimgate that calls cpPmden() and returns the density vector to R.  It is
GPL (>= 3).

The file src/cpp11.cpp is auto-generated by cpp11 (MIT licence, auto-generated
registration boilerplate) and is not modified by stimgate.

Modifications made for integration into stimgate:
- Removed FAUST-specific includes (faust.h was replaced by a minimal header).
- Added a maximum-iteration guard (`cpPmden_max_iter = 10000`) to the outer
  `while (stillRepeating)` loop in `cpPmden.cpp` to prevent infinite loops on
  edge-case inputs (e.g. near-uniform data).  This corresponds to the `MAXIT`
  parameter present in the original ftnonpar FORTRAN source `pmden.f`.
- No other algorithmic changes were made to any ported function.
